\fs24
\b APB UART IP Micro-Architecture\b0\par
\par
\b 1. Module Partitioning\b0\par
The APB UART IP is split into modular RTL blocks:\par
- \b apb_uart_top\b0 : top wrapper that instantiates and connects all submodules.\par
- \b uart_ctrl_apb\b0 : APB register/control logic (DATA/STATUS/CTRL/BAUD).\par
- \b uart_tx\b0 : UART transmitter state machine and serial output generation.\par
- \b uart_rx\b0 : UART receiver state machine and byte reconstruction.\par
- \b uart_fifo\b0 : external reusable FIFO module used for TX FIFO and RX FIFO.\par
- \b apb_uart\b0 : compatibility wrapper around apb_uart_top.\par
\par
\b 2. External Interface\b0\par
APB: pclk, presetn, psel, penable, pwrite, paddr, pwdata, prdata, pready, pslverr.\par
UART: uart_tx, uart_rx.\par
Flow control: cts_i, rts_o.\par
Interrupt: irq.\par
\par
\b 3. Register Map (uart_ctrl_apb)\b0\par
0x00 DATA: write TX byte, read RX byte.\par
0x04 STATUS: FIFO flags/levels and flow-control visibility.\par
0x08 CTRL: uart_en, tx_en, rx_en, irq_en.\par
0x0C BAUD: baud_div (zero ignored).\par
\par
\b 4. Data Path\b0\par
- APB writes feed TX FIFO through uart_ctrl_apb.\par
- uart_tx pops TX FIFO when cts_i is asserted and serializes 8N1 frame on uart_tx.\par
- uart_rx deserializes uart_rx into bytes and pushes RX FIFO when valid.\par
- APB reads pop RX FIFO through uart_ctrl_apb.\par
\par
\b 5. Flow Control\b0\par
- cts_i gates TX frame launch in uart_tx.\par
- rts_o is generated in top wrapper from RX FIFO occupancy (headroom-based threshold).\par
\par
\b 6. Clock/Reset and IRQ\b0\par
- Shared baud generator in top wrapper drives uart_tx and uart_rx baud_tick.\par
- Active-low reset initializes control registers, FIFOs, and FSM states.\par
- irq is generated in uart_ctrl_apb from FIFO status and irq_en.\par
}
